# Sticky site footer

The site footer / bottom banner (`SiteFooter`) must **always** sit at the **bottom of the viewport**, never floating in the middle of short pages.

## Required pattern

1. Root layout `body`: `min-h-dvh flex flex-col` (not only `min-h-full`).
2. Page shell wrapping header + main + footer: `min-h-dvh flex flex-col`.
3. Main content area: `flex-1` (grows to fill remaining space).
4. Footer: `mt-auto` (or rely on flex-1 main pushing it down).

## Do not

- Place the footer directly under short content so empty space sits **below** the footer.
- Use height chains that collapse (`h-full` / `min-h-full` alone without a viewport minimum).

## When adding pages

Any new page that includes `SiteFooter` must follow this shell. Prefer reusing existing page shells (`ForgeHome`, pricing clients, `MySharesPage`) rather than inventing a new layout.
